{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QDEH8pja9jpupkrmbcWD2v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review ARR review form 2025 2026 overall assessment scoring scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 October | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FOctober\"},{\"title\":\"ACLRollingReview (@ReviewAcl) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/ReviewAcl\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) assessment scoring system:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. \n\nWhile the search results indicate that a scoring system exists for the 2025 cycles, the specific 1-5 scale definitions for the overall assessment are not fully detailed in the official ARR documentation I found. However, one forum discussion references Overall Assessment scores, mentioning that \"5.0 Award-worthy (top 2.5%)\" and \"4.0\" are categories in the assessment hierarchy.\n\nFor more detailed information about the complete scoring scale definitions (1-5) for overall assessment, you may want to visit the official ARR review form at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or the ARR reviewer guidelines at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines, which appear to contain the full scoring rubric.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cac5a696-6b6e-48ad-ab92-08181aa0595a","uuid":"37d63a79-73f3-4608-8ec6-9dbd590da3ac","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:55:51.550Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review ARR review form 2025 2026 overall assessment scoring scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JdDmtVTT6kn3ANfz2U2Ra9","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F202