{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019UKy5FGUtuzP2rHM9Gj3A2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016QX3qX4HT2m9dN11vN1kDv","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform soundness excitement overall recommendation scale"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2310,"cache_read_input_tokens":62441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2310},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cac5a696-6b6e-48ad-ab92-08181aa0595a","uuid":"fc15d776-cac9-48b0-841c-84ab5e2b5c27"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016QX3qX4HT2m9dN11vN1kDv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform soundness excitement overall recommendation scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"Submission Form Fields\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/submissionform\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Beware: Common Submission Problems\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authorchecklist\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) scoring system:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHere's how each score is defined:\n\n**Soundness:** The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. The soundness scale evaluates whether papers are sufficiently sound and thorough, with ratings ranging from 5 (Excellent) to 3 (Acceptable), among others.\n\n**Excitement:** Excitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n**Overall Recommendation:** The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nThe search results indicate that while soundness and excitement are distinct dimensions, the overall recommendation integrates these along with other considerations like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cac5a696-6b6e-48ad-ab92-08181aa0595a","uuid":"56aa5f7c-f95d-43d1-bd27-ab9018080185","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:56:05.735Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform soundness excitement overall recommendation scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018nc8onEsimJTzZRZVEwYBa","content":[{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Response to ACL 2023 Questions","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Changelog","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"Incentives 2026","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"Submission Form Fields","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/submissionform"},{"title":"Authors Beware: Common Submission Problems","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authorchecklist"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) scoring system:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHere's how each score is defined:\n\n**Soundness:** The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. The soundness scale evaluates whether papers are sufficiently sound and thorough, with ratings ranging from 5 (Excellent) to 3 (Acceptable), among others.\n\n**Excitement:** Excitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n**Overall Recommendation:** The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nThe search results indicate that while soundness and excitement are distinct dimensions, the overall recommendation integrates these along with other considerations like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":6.983980800000005}}
