{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014nQDUb4Vxx7xdoij9W1FC5","type":"tool_result","content":"# ACL Rolling Review Scoring Scales\n\n## Soundness\n- **5**: \"Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\"\n- **4**: \"Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims.\"\n- **3**: \"Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\"\n- **2**: \"Poor: Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported.\"\n- **1**: \"Major Issues: This study is not yet sufficiently thorough to warrant publication.\"\n\n## Excitement\n- **5**: \"Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation.\"\n- **4**: \"Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend.\"\n- **3**: \"Interesting: I might mention some points of this paper to others and/or attend if time permits.\"\n- **2**: \"Potentially Interesting: this paper does not resonate with me, but might with others.\"\n- **1**: \"Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others.\"\n\n## Overall Assessment/Recommendation\n- **5**: \"Consider for Award: Could be considered for an outstanding paper award.\"\n- **4**: \"Conference: Could be accepted to an *ACL conference.\"\n- **3**: \"Findings: Could be accepted to the Findings of the ACL.\"\n- **2**: \"Resubmit next cycle: Needs substantial revisions completable by next cycle.\"\n- **1**: \"Do not resubmit: Paper has to be fully redone or lacks relevance.\"\n\n## Other Scored Dimensions\n- **Reviewer Confidence** (1-5 scale)\n- **Reproducibility** (1-5 scale)\n- **Datasets** (1-5 scale)\n- **Software** (1-5 scale)\n- **Author Identity Knowledge** (1-5 scale)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cac5a696-6b6e-48ad-ab92-08181aa0595a","uuid":"466f6828-b0fb-45d9-a6e8-40a47686f913","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:56:24.889Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":25365,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# ACL Rolling Review Scoring Scales\n\n## Soundness\n- **5**: \"Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\"\n- **4**: \"Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims.\"\n- **3**: \"Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\"\n- **2**: \"Poor: Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported.\"\n- **1**: \"Major Issues: This study is not yet sufficiently thorough to warrant publication.\"\n\n## Excitement\n- **5**: \"Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation.\"\n- **4**: \"Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend.\"\n- **3**: \"Interesting: I might mention some points of this paper to others and/or attend if time permits.\"\n- **2**: \"Potentially Interesting: this paper does not resonate with me, but might with others.\"\n- **1**: \"Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others.\"\n\n## Overall Assessment/Recommendation\n- **5**: \"Consider for Award: Could be considered for an outstanding paper award.\"\n- **4**: \"Conference: Could be accepted to an *ACL conference.\"\n- **3**: \"Findings: Could be accepted to the Findings of the ACL.\"\n- **2**: \"Resubmit next cycle: Needs substantial revisions completable by next cycle.\"\n- **1**: \"Do not resubmit: Paper has to be fully redone or lacks relevance.\"\n\n## Other Scored Dimensions\n- **Reviewer Confidence** (1-5 scale)\n- **Reproducibility** (1-5 scale)\n- **Datasets** (1-5 scale)\n- **Software** (1-5 scale)\n- **Author Identity Knowledge** (1-5 scale)","durationMs":5566,"url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019onBdh9YRcVkCNEDm1qtpv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the ARR review form scoring scales. The Insights from Negative Results workshop is an ACL workshop that likely uses a similar review form (possibly simplified for workshop papers). Since this is a workshop for negative results, the criteria emphasize:\n1. Whether the negative result is informative/insightful\n2. Whether the experimental methodology is sound\n3. Whether the paper provides useful lessons for the community\n\nLet me also fetch the workshop CFP for more specific criteria.\n\nNow I have all the information I need to conduct the review. Let me now dispatch the two reviewers and then do the roundtable synthesis.\n\nThe task says to use the `dream-review-full` skill dispatch template with 2 Reviewers:\n\n\n- R1 focusing on Methods + Experiments\n- R2 focusing on Novelty + Related Work\n\nI'll run them in parallel, then move through the roundtable process: independent reviews first, then cross-sharing, converging on key points, and finally synthesizing into a coherent assessment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":578,"cache_read_input_tokens":66239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":578},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cac5a696-6b6e-48ad-ab92-08181aa0595a","uuid":"038f0126-ef44-42bc-bf42-043525da2a19"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019onBdh9YRcVkCNEDm1qtpv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the ARR scoring scales and workshop context. Now launching R1 (Methods + Experiments) and R2 (Novelty + Related Work) in parallel for independent review."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":578,"cache_read_input_tokens":66239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":578},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cac5a696-6b6e-48ad-ab92-08181aa0595a","uuid":"c8970814-c035-49be-bdd8-bc19d56b1112"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019onBdh9YRcVkCNEDm1qtpv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R2j8yrXHw6d35UTJKxEpU2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for an academic paper review. Your focus area is **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Venue\nInsights from Negative Results in NLP workshop @ EMNLP 2026. This workshop publishes short papers (up to 4 pages + references) reporting negative or unexpected results that provide insights for the NLP/ML community. The workshop values: (1) informative negative results, (2) sound methodology, (3) useful lessons/insights.\n\n## Scoring Scale (ARR format)\n- Soundness: 1-5 (1=Major Issues, 2=Poor, 3=Acceptable, 4=Strong, 5=Excellent)\n- Excitement: 1-5 (1=Not Exciting, 2=Potentially Interesting, 3=Interesting, 4=Exciting, 5=Highly Exciting)\n- Overall: 1-5 (1=Do not resubmit, 2=Resubmit next cycle, 3=Findings, 4=Conference, 5=Award-worthy)\n- Confidence: 1-5\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"Error Injection Helps Tool-Use but Hurts Planning: Boundary Conditions for Failure-Augmented Agent Training\"\n\nThe paper tests whether taxonomy-guided error injection (a core component of PALADIN, which works well for tool-use agents on ToolBench) transfers to embodied planning. They design TaxEI, a 4-operator error taxonomy for ALFWorld, and train Qwen3-8B under 3 conditions: Vanilla (clean only), TaxEI (taxonomy-tagged injections), Random (unlabeled injections). Key findings:\n- TaxEI degrades mean performance by 8.6pp (56.7% vs 65.3%, p≈0.32) with 2.6× variance increase\n- Primary effect is training instability, not systematic degradation (2/3 seeds match Vanilla, 1 collapses)\n- Variance gradient: Vanilla SD < Random SD < TaxEI SD — consistent across environments, scales\n- WebShop replication confirms directional consistency with attenuated effects\n- Scale ablation to 50K narrows but doesn't close gap (-5.4pp, p≈0.09)\n- Qualitative failure analysis reveals noise-induced incoherence + taxonomy-specific error echoes\n- Per-operator analysis shows error locality gradient matching macro-level environment gradient\n\n## Experiment Design Context (from review_context.yaml)\nThe paper covers 6 experiments in its \"imagined\" design:\n1. Training Dynamics Analysis — loss decomposition by sample type\n2. Second Environment Replication (WebShop) — cross-environment generalization\n3. Qualitative Failure Analysis — 25 TaxEI failure cases classified into 4 types\n4. Scale Ablation (25K/50K) — testing PALADIN-scale data\n5. Recovery Prompting (5-shot in-context) — inference-time vs training-time delivery\n6. Per-Operator Recovery Deep Dive — 3-seed per-operator patterns\n\nThe narrative guidance says results are in \"marginal significance\" territory, with the contribution framed as a \"cautionary negative result\" with directional warnings rather than precise quantitative boundaries. Most p-values fall in 0.05-0.20 range.\n\n## Your Task (R1: Methods + Experiments)\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n\n1. **Experimental Design Adequacy**: Are the 3 conditions (Vanilla/TaxEI/Random) well-controlled? Is the comparison with PALADIN fair? Are the 6 supplementary experiments well-motivated?\n\n2. **Statistical Rigor**: 3 seeds × 47 tasks — is this sufficient? How should we interpret p-values in the 0.05-0.32 range? Is the paper honest about statistical limitations?\n\n3. **Methodology Issues**: \n   - Data generation: 501 trajectories from GPT-5.2, 4,671 injected variants. Is this pipeline sound?\n   - Training: Qwen3-8B SFT with 3 conditions. Any concerns about the training setup?\n   - Evaluation: ALFWorld 47-task test set + WebShop. Sufficient?\n   - Dose-response ablation is single-seed only. How problematic?\n\n4. **Coverage vs Design Context**: The paper reports 6 supplementary experiments. Are they sufficient? What's missing?\n\n5. **Specific Strengths and Weaknesses** (as bullet lists)\n\n6. **Questions for Authors** (2-3 specific questions)\n\n7. **Scores** with brief justification:\n   - Soundness: X/5\n   - Excitement: X/5\n   - Overall: X/5\n   - Confidence: X/5\n\nWrite your review in structured format with clear section headings. Be rigorous but fair — this is a negative results workshop, so evaluate whether the negative result is well-established and informative, not whether the method achieves SOTA."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":578,"cache_read_input_tokens":66239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":578},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cac5a696-6b6e-48ad-ab92-08181aa0595a","uuid":"ea31e7ef-a450-4360-834d-70300173435f"}
